#!/usr/bin/env ruby

# This script pre-generates the images for the Hour of AI 2026 Sprite Lab
# image levels, for the lab's image cache (imageCache.ts in apps/).
#
# A student describes an image by filling a sentence with words: "A
# [adjective] [creature] wearing a [clothing]". This script draws every way
# each sentence can be filled, VARIANTS times, checks each drawing with the
# same moderation the lab applies to a live one, and publishes the ones that
# pass to the tree the lab reads from.
#
# PROMPTS:
#
# The prompts are not built here. dump_prompts.ts imports the lab's prompt
# builders and prints one job per filled sentence; this script runs it via
# `npx tsx`, so the words the model gets are the lab's. It needs Node 18 or
# newer. The words come from sentences.json beside this script, a pinned
# copy of the lab's: see README.md.
#
# MODERATION:
#
# The lab runs no safety check on a cached image, so this script is the only
# one an image gets. Azure AI Content Safety checks every frame, always;
# --judge adds aichat's LLM judges, on every frame and every prompt. A
# flagged variant is redrawn up to MAX_REDRAWS times, then left out. Nothing
# without a passing verdict is published.
#
# USAGE:
#
# See the words, and the size of a run:
#
# ./bin/oneoff/hoai_2026/imagegen/generate_images --list-words
# ./bin/oneoff/hoai_2026/imagegen/generate_images --list-sentences
#
# Draw and check everything not yet drawn (thousands of requests):
#
# ./bin/oneoff/hoai_2026/imagegen/generate_images
#
# Review with review_images, then publish: --no-dry-run to the devel
# bucket, then --no-dry-run --production, which publishes only variants
# approved in review.
#
# Nothing in this script deletes an image. A variant that is redrawn, after
# moderation flags it or review rejects it, moves to image_attic first.

